    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333687/comment/12379733",
          "id": "12379733",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oleg.kalnichevski%40bearingpoint.com",
            "name": "oleg.kalnichevski@bearingpoint.com",
            "key": "oleg.kalnichevski@bearingpoint.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10453",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10453",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10453",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10453"
            },
            "displayName": "oleg.kalnichevski@bearingpoint.com",
            "active": false,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I strongly disagree it's HttpClient's responsibility to check what type of URL \na request is redirected to. I do not think the HttpClient should take liberty \nin changing a request type, matter how appropriate that might seem at the first \nglance. This kind of decision should better be taken on a higher level, that \nis, by the HttpClient consumer",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oleg.kalnichevski%40bearingpoint.com",
            "name": "oleg.kalnichevski@bearingpoint.com",
            "key": "oleg.kalnichevski@bearingpoint.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10453",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10453",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10453",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10453"
            },
            "displayName": "oleg.kalnichevski@bearingpoint.com",
            "active": false,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2002-11-21T23:20:58.000+0000",
          "updated": "2002-11-21T23:20:58.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333687/comment/12379734",
          "id": "12379734",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=toemmi",
            "name": "toemmi",
            "key": "toemmi",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mathis",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "I agree with you that the HttpClient should not check what kind of URL the \nredirect is. But please take once more a look to the RFC (10.3 Redirection \n3xx). The second request (forwarded method) can only be a GET or HEAD. POST is \nnot allowed.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=toemmi",
            "name": "toemmi",
            "key": "toemmi",
            "avatarUrls": {
